      "writtenOn": "2022-08-10T07:21:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed this looks weird, I\u0027ll try a patch to remove the \"--jars\".\n\nFor arguments like --apistubs that are repeated in the command-line, it seems doing `--apistubs foo --apistubs bar` works too and is more conventional, so I\u0027ll update the makefiles to do that.\n\n`--unsupportedapi` takes a list of files fed from the genrule with a filegroup though, and the genrule outputs a space-separated list: `--unsupportedapi $(locations :unsupported-api-files)`. I\u0027d have to do pretty ugly hacks to convert this to another syntax, maybe something like:\n\n    genrule {\n      cmd: \"$(location :gen_jarjar) \" +\n        [...]\n        \" `printf -- \u0027--unsupportedapi %s \u0027 $(locations \"unsupported-api-files)` \" +\n        [...]\n    }\n\nThat\u0027s a lot less clear, so maybe it\u0027s better to keep the space-separated list for that argument ?",
      "parentUuid": "4d0d4da5_63c2395d",
      "range": {
